Implement the following plan:

# Survey Builder: Enhanced Animations and Visible Delete Button

## Context
The user wants to improve the survey builder UX with:
1. Better drop area visualization showing where items will be placed
2. Animated movement of existing items when hovering over drop positions
3. Visible delete button directly on canvas items (not hidden in a menu)

## Current Implementation
- Uses `@dnd-kit` for drag-and-drop and `framer-motion` for animations
- Drop indicator is a simple dashed border box
- Delete button is hidden in a DropdownMenu (requires two clicks)

---

## Implementation Plan

### Task 1: Visible Delete Button on Question Cards

**File:** `apps/web/src/components/survey-builder/question-card.tsx`

1. Remove `DropdownMenu` wrapper around delete action
2. Add visible delete `Button` that appears on card hover
3. Add confirmation state (click once to reveal confirm, click again to delete)

```tsx
// Add state
const [showDeleteConfirm, setShowDeleteConfirm] = useState(false);

// Add 'group' class to Card for hover states
<Card className={cn("cursor-pointer transition-all group", ...)}>

// Replace DropdownMenu with direct delete button
{showDeleteConfirm ? (
  <div className="flex items-center gap-1">
    <Button variant="ghost" size="icon" onClick={() => setShowDeleteConfirm(false)}>
      <X className="h-4 w-4" />
    </Button>
    <Button variant="ghost" size="icon" className="text-red-600" onClick={() => deleteMutation.mutate({ id: question.id })}>
      <Trash2 className="h-4 w-4" />
    </Button>
  </div>
) : (
  <Button
    variant="ghost"
    size="icon"
    className="opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 data-[selected=true]:opacity-100"
    onClick={() => setShowDeleteConfirm(true)}
  >
    <Trash2 className="h-4 w-4" />
  </Button>
)}
```

---

### Task 2: Enhanced Drop Indicator

**File:** `apps/web/src/components/survey-builder/builder-canvas.tsx`

1. Enhance `DropIndicator` with animated glow effect
2. Show the question type being dragged
3. Add height animation for smooth insertion

```tsx
interface DropIndicatorProps {
  questionType?: Question["type"];
}

function DropIndicator({ questionType }: DropIndicatorProps) {
  return (
    <motion.div
      initial={{ opacity: 0, height: 0 }}
      animate={{ opacity: 1, height: "auto" }}
      exit={{ opacity: 0, height: 0 }}
      className="overflow-hidden"
    >
      <div className="relative flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border-2 border-violet-500 bg-violet-50 p-4">
        {/* Animated glow */}
        <motion.div
          className="absolute inset-0 rounded-xl border-2 border-violet-400"
          animate={{ opacity: [0.3, 0.7, 0.3] }}
          transition={{ duration: 1.5, repeat: Infinity }}
        />
        <Plus className="h-5 w-5 text-violet-600" />
        <span className="font-medium text-violet-700">
          Drop to add {questionTypeLabels[questionType]}
        </span>
      </div>
    </motion.div>
  );
}
```

---

### Task 3: Animated Item Displacement

**File:** `apps/web/src/components/survey-builder/builder-canvas.tsx`

1. Wrap questions in `LayoutGroup` for coordinated animations
2. Add `layout` prop to question card motion.div wrappers
3. Animate existing items to shift when hovering over drop position

```tsx
import { LayoutGroup } from "framer-motion";

// In render, wrap SortableContext with LayoutGroup
<LayoutGroup>
  <SortableContext items={safeQuestions.map(q => q.id)} strategy={verticalListSortingStrategy}>
    {safeQuestions.map((question, index) => {
      // Calculate if this item should shift down
      const shouldShift = isOver && activeDragItem?.type === "palette" && index >= dropIndex;

      return (
        <motion.div
          key={question.id}
          layout
          animate={{ y: shouldShift ? 80 : 0 }}
          transition={{ type: "spring", stiffness: 400, damping: 30 }}
        >
          <QuestionCard ... />
        </motion.div>
      );
    })}
  </SortableContext>
</LayoutGroup>
```

---

## Critical Files
- `apps/web/src/components/survey-builder/question-card.tsx` - Delete button visibility
- `apps/web/src/components/survey-builder/builder-canvas.tsx` - Drop indicator and layout animations

---

## Verification
- [ ] Delete button visible on card hover and when selected
- [ ] Delete requires two clicks (confirm state prevents accidents)
- [ ] Drop indicator shows animated glow and question type
- [ ] Existing questions smoothly shift when dragging over drop position
- [ ] Animations are smooth with 10+ questions
- [ ] Mobile/touch interactions still work


If you need specific details from before exiting plan mode (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/orksys/.REDACTED.jsonl

If this plan can be broken down into multiple independent tasks, consider using the TeamCreate tool to create a team and parallelize the work.

